  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PublicPrivate Infrastructure Advisory Facility (PPIAF) NonCore Fund as a Response to the Global Financial Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;PPIAF&apos;s general objectives are to help developing countries improve the  quality of their infrastructure services through private sector  involvement.  This particular TF supplements this objective by  providing an additional implementation mechanism for projects that  arose because of the global financial crisis; it will accommodate the  donors&apos; requirement to earmark funds to these crisis-response  activities and will facilitate appropriate monitoring and reporting  separate from the PPIAF core program.
 PPIAF&apos;s objective are to: a) mobilize and leverage donor resources;  exploit the expertise and economies of scale and scope
 available from an integratedcomma multi-donor work program; promote the  exchange of lessons of experience between sectorscomma
 regions and donors; facilitate coordination between bilateral and  multilateral programs addressing the same concerns.
 Impacts of the current financial crisis are especially damaging to the  sector because infrastructure services are key drivers
 of economic growth and poverty alleviation.Increased infrastructure  investment will be a key stimulus needed to help countries recover as  quickly as possible from the anticipated global recession. PPIAF  support is becoming more critical to help country governments weather  the current financial crisis and its implications for infrastructure  development.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
